---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About — Eran Gamage"
  description="About Eran Gamage, a physics-trained master's student and researcher in data science working across AI systems, retrieval, energy analytics, and privacy-preserving protocols."
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl space-y-5">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white md:text-5xl">
      Physics background, data science practice.
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">
      I’m a master’s student and researcher in data science with a physics background from the University of Colombo and current work connected to RMIT. I like problems where modelling, systems thinking, and careful evaluation all matter.
    </p>
    <p class="leading-8 text-slate-300">
      My recent work sits around retrieval-augmented generation, NLP evaluation, Australian energy grid analytics, and privacy-preserving retrieval ideas for blockchain systems. I’m interested in building systems that are understandable, reproducible, and useful beyond a demo.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
    <article class="card">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">What I study</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-300">
        Machine learning, retrieval systems, time-series modelling, and data pipelines for real-world datasets.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">What I value</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-300">
        Clear baselines, grounded claims, readable code, and results that can be checked by someone else.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">What I’m exploring</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-300">
        Practical AI systems for decision support, energy data, and privacy-aware access to information.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
